# =============================================================================
# OpenS100 - Git attributes
#
# Purpose
#   1. Disable automatic end-of-line conversion so that the currently committed
#      content is frozen exactly as it is.
#   2. Protect encoding-sensitive files (such as .rc) from being altered by Git.
#
# Background
#   - The blobs in this repository already contain CRLF, while the development
#     environment has core.autocrlf=true. Under that combination, editing a file
#     makes Git renormalize the whole file to LF, producing a large diff that has
#     nothing to do with the actual change.
#   - The `* -text` rule below takes precedence over core.autocrlf and disables
#     EOL conversion for the entire repository. Files are stored exactly as they
#     are and checked out exactly as they were stored.
#
# Note
#   The source encoding policy (UTF-8 with BOM) is enforced by the compiler
#   settings and a validation script, not by Git. See OpenS100.Common.props and
#   CONVENTIONS.md.
# =============================================================================

# Default: no EOL conversion (freeze the current state)
* -text

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resource files
#   The MFC resource editor saves these as UTF-16LE. If Git mistakes them for
#   text and converts or merges them, the files are corrupted. Treat as binary.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.rc      binary
*.rc2     binary

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets (prevent diff/merge attempts)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png     binary
*.bmp     binary
*.ico     binary
*.ttf     binary
*.eap     binary
*.lib     binary
*.dll     binary
*.exe     binary
*.pdb     binary
*.h5      binary
*.000     binary

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual Studio project files
#   Structured XML/INI formats; conflicts are safer to resolve by hand.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sln          -text
*.vcxproj      -text
*.vcxproj.filters -text
*.props        -text
